{"chapter": "stacks", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "0268", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:57073ae02bda040e85875a2efa042314529165a87a9d72a96363977fd6ab0792", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nHere is the definition of a stack. It mixes the notion of a fibred\ncategory with the notion of descent.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:c86fa2a0f10a4424d5b5578f9fd9cac376ca11528ed974c43b0dd0b042c21005", "unit_id": "tag:0268:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "stacks", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "0268", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0003": "$p : \\mathcal{S} \\to \\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0005": "$p : \\mathcal{S} \\to \\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0006": "$U \\in \\Ob(\\mathcal{C})$", "MATH_0007": "$x, y \\in \\mathcal{S}_U$", "MATH_0008": "$\\mathit{Mor}(x, y)$", "MATH_0009": "$\\mathcal{C}/U$", "MATH_0010": "$\\mathcal{U} = \\{f_i : U_i \\to U\\}_{i \\in I}$", "MATH_0011": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0012": "$\\mathcal{S}$", "MATH_0013": "$\\mathcal{U}$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{categories-definition-fibred-category}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{definition-mor-presheaf}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\item", "STRUCT_0005": "\\end{enumerate}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-stack}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:2a8be13f1965fd887e2f8e3757b1072dc83e36c4f84993a12ac20aa372e138ce", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:3d9f46fdd50e1d4159b98b33162fd0458bb2faf34869a25ea7674395bfb9cda6", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a site. A <TEXTITOPEN_0001>stack<TEXTITCLOSE_0001> over <MATH_0002>\nis a category <MATH_0003> over <MATH_0004> which\nsatisfies the following conditions:\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> <MATH_0005> is a fibred category, see\nCategories, Definition <REF_0001>,\n<STRUCT_0003> for any <MATH_0006> and any <MATH_0007>\nthe presheaf <MATH_0008> (see\nDefinition <REF_0002>) is a sheaf on\nthe site <MATH_0009>, and\n<STRUCT_0004> for any covering <MATH_0010>\nof the site <MATH_0011>, any descent datum in <MATH_0012>\nrelative to <MATH_0013> is effective.\n<STRUCT_0005>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:df7b3ae8d7fa7f24f130faf23f8bdeccda6e662597f7fa939b96e06b349db9b8", "unit_id": "tag:026F:statement"}
{"chapter": "stacks", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "0268", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent", "STRUCT_0002": "\\medskip", "STRUCT_0003": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:60933e2eb73b5869424ecf69d90b96f339f85ff45ff143b7b9fe9b3e0ad8de56", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:8ffc0d584b85acbc2d9544fcba568eea09d049ce2340b0e2fb3c8deadab1d570", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nWe find the formulation above the most convenient way to think about\na stack. Namely, given a category over <MATH_0001> in order to verify\nthat it is a stack you proceed to check properties (1), (2) and\n(3) in that order. Certainly properties (2) and (3) do not make sense\nif the category isn't fibred. Without (2) we cannot prove that the\ndescent in (3) is unique up to unique isomorphism and functorial.\n\n<STRUCT_0002><STRUCT_0003>\nThe following lemma provides an alternative definition.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:d842b79fe1659fa6a4d414ee01daaa9d0abecd75625455084f5b3dcf7d12ee87", "unit_id": "tag:0268:prose-0002"}
{"chapter": "stacks", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "0268", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0002": "$p : \\mathcal{S} \\to \\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{S}$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{U} = \\{f_i : U_i \\to U\\}_{i \\in I}$", "MATH_0007": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0008": "$$\n\\mathcal{S}_U \\longrightarrow DD(\\mathcal{U})\n$$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-stack-equivalences}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:9b8415ea52c394b9960a6159ed213ad6514242713e274dc71f02ab7a06a7dff0", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:d879cfa4cbfbaea30cfd4cbf0b4fa82c769563ed26ab3a08e7ad7f5afce99afd", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a site.\nLet <MATH_0002> be a fibred category\nover <MATH_0003>. The following are equivalent\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> <MATH_0004> is a stack over <MATH_0005>, and\n<STRUCT_0003> for any covering <MATH_0006>\nof the site <MATH_0007> the functor\n<MATH_0008>\nwhich associates to an\nobject its canonical descent datum is an equivalence.\n<STRUCT_0004>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:5e988f60a76401ad3ce675d2ea8e25ee8cd5b7fdda60262407aa83049da2b0ec", "unit_id": "tag:02ZF:statement"}
{"chapter": "stacks", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "0268", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:51c14ae31949a9d2fc04929bff10bb80f9a99f3167d38ffcd4bc71a589e1a114", "source_text": "Omitted.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:872a8cfa74892c6e6464bd864d9f1c292f4f523caba3e51ac3dafbfc84db48f6", "unit_id": "tag:02ZF:proof"}
{"chapter": "stacks", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "0268", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$p : \\mathcal{S} \\to \\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{S}'$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{S}$", "MATH_0005": "$\\varphi : y \\to x$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{S}$", "MATH_0007": "$x$", "MATH_0008": "$\\mathcal{S}'$", "MATH_0009": "$y$", "MATH_0010": "$\\mathcal{S}'$", "MATH_0011": "$\\mathcal{S}'$", "MATH_0012": "$\\mathcal{S}$", "MATH_0013": "$\\{f_i : U_i \\to U\\}$", "MATH_0014": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0015": "$x$", "MATH_0016": "$\\mathcal{S}$", "MATH_0017": "$U$", "MATH_0018": "$f_i^*x$", "MATH_0019": "$\\mathcal{S}'$", "MATH_0020": "$i$", "MATH_0021": "$x$", "MATH_0022": "$\\mathcal{S}'$", "MATH_0023": "$\\mathcal{S}' \\to \\mathcal{C}$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\item", "STRUCT_0005": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-substack}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:8ebb9f1f1e400334da02b6355304c8c2f560d61bd0d1130b9cdc8b38774e4cf4", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:8c508f4e2bb72886ea24eb5bbbf4f11355b5bc212d55246773653913cadd5eeb", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a stack over the site <MATH_0002>.\nLet <MATH_0003> be a subcategory of <MATH_0004>.\nAssume\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> if <MATH_0005> is a strongly cartesian\nmorphism of <MATH_0006> and\n<MATH_0007> is an object of <MATH_0008>, then <MATH_0009> is isomorphic to an\nobject of <MATH_0010>,\n<STRUCT_0003> <MATH_0011> is a full subcategory of <MATH_0012>, and\n<STRUCT_0004> if <MATH_0013> is a covering of <MATH_0014>,\nand <MATH_0015> an object of <MATH_0016> over <MATH_0017> such that <MATH_0018>\nis isomorphic to an object of <MATH_0019> for each <MATH_0020>,\nthen <MATH_0021> is isomorphic to an object of <MATH_0022>.\n<STRUCT_0005>\nThen <MATH_0023> is a stack.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:b49da24df26aeacca9c206307e195537b7c2b0363948ba13d377f24baa5a804f", "unit_id": "tag:04TU:statement"}
{"chapter": "stacks", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "0268", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{S}'$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathit{Isom}$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{S}'$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{S}$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{S}'$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{S}$", "MATH_0007": "$\\mathcal{S}'$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:7f157eb7170f5dc275af944c6a848efa7ff7fbe3df20fe87bb106bb747e09b51", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:86ee0c15ddf7e59f0e73c76e1e32ff89ec7353aa6e1aa56b8630fafe6cc492b2", "source_text": "Omitted. Hints:\nThe first condition guarantees that <MATH_0001> is a fibred category.\nThe second condition guarantees that the <MATH_0002>-presheaves\nof <MATH_0003> are sheaves (as they are identical to their counter parts\nin <MATH_0004>). The third condition guarantees that the descent condition\nholds in <MATH_0005> as we can first descend in <MATH_0006> and\nthen (3) implies the resulting object is isomorphic to an object of\n<MATH_0007>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:3dd5e10a844928ec18cacea5084b4b31bcea396a044881b89edc037cdc882257", "unit_id": "tag:04TU:proof"}
{"chapter": "stacks", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "0268", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{S}_1$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{S}_2$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{S}_1$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{S}_2$", "MATH_0007": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0008": "$\\mathcal{S}_1$", "MATH_0009": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0010": "$\\mathcal{S}_2$", "MATH_0011": "$\\mathcal{C}$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-stack-equivalent}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:7a06d8cecc2e4ffe3e65ef19e939456917e6e4d2d4b8b74b82b626d9d5802132", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:060a83135c0173598ee975906680347eda8bb998163cac2a536947b0b6f037c2", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a site.\nLet <MATH_0002>, <MATH_0003> be categories over <MATH_0004>.\nSuppose that <MATH_0005> and <MATH_0006> are equivalent\nas categories over <MATH_0007>.\nThen <MATH_0008> is a stack over <MATH_0009> if and only if\n<MATH_0010> is a stack over <MATH_0011>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:bf9134f8e8dbfb38c4d3e5431b6973266cd3a44e29135916d1f671742506dfc0", "unit_id": "tag:042W:statement"}
{"chapter": "stacks", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "0268", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$F : \\mathcal{S}_1 \\to \\mathcal{S}_2$", "MATH_0002": "$G : \\mathcal{S}_2 \\to \\mathcal{S}_1$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0004": "$i : F \\circ G \\to \\text{id}_{\\mathcal{S}_2}$", "MATH_0005": "$j : G \\circ F \\to \\text{id}_{\\mathcal{S}_1}$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0007": "$\\mathcal{S}_1$", "MATH_0008": "$\\mathcal{S}_2$", "MATH_0009": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0010": "$\\mathcal{S}_1$", "MATH_0011": "$\\mathcal{S}_2$", "MATH_0012": "$F$", "MATH_0013": "$G$", "MATH_0014": "$F$", "MATH_0015": "$G$", "MATH_0016": "$1$", "MATH_0017": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0018": "$U \\in \\Ob(\\mathcal{C})$", "MATH_0019": "$x, y \\in \\mathcal{S}_{1, U}$", "MATH_0020": "$$\n\\mathit{Mor}_{\\mathcal{S}_1}(x, y),\n\\mathit{Mor}_{\\mathcal{S}_1}(F(x), F(y)) :\n(\\mathcal{C}/U)^{opp} \\longrightarrow \\textit{Sets}.\n$$", "MATH_0021": "$\\mathcal{S}_1$", "MATH_0022": "$\\mathcal{S}_2$", "MATH_0023": "$(X_i, \\varphi_{ii'})$", "MATH_0024": "$\\mathcal{S}_2$", "MATH_0025": "$\\{U_i \\to U\\}$", "MATH_0026": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0027": "$(G(X_i), G(\\varphi_{ii'}))$", "MATH_0028": "$\\mathcal{S}_1$", "MATH_0029": "$\\{U_i \\to U\\}$", "MATH_0030": "$X$", "MATH_0031": "$\\mathcal{S}_{1, U}$", "MATH_0032": "$(f_i^*X, can)$", "MATH_0033": "$(G(X_i), G(\\varphi_{ii'}))$", "MATH_0034": "$F(X)$", "MATH_0035": "$\\mathcal{S}_{2, U}$", "MATH_0036": "$(f_i^*F(X), can)$", "MATH_0037": "$(F(G(X_i)), F(G(\\varphi_{ii'})))$", "MATH_0038": "$(X_i, \\varphi_{ii'})$", "MATH_0039": "$i$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{categories-lemma-fibred-equivalent}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{categories-lemma-fibred-equivalent}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{lemma-presheaf-mor-map-fibred-categories}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:56a4bf47fa7078c8d076246cc2c1925fd747a2f18145fb028195343b82dbd396", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:9a9fa1ff632cab298addf36d60e1400a1860703162df79f2271d6aa90511ed19", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001>,\n<MATH_0002> be functors over <MATH_0003>, and let\n<MATH_0004>,\n<MATH_0005> be isomorphisms of\nfunctors over <MATH_0006>. By\nCategories, Lemma <REF_0001>\nwe see that <MATH_0007> is fibred if and only if <MATH_0008>\nis fibred over <MATH_0009>. Hence we may assume that both\n<MATH_0010> and <MATH_0011> are fibred. Moreover, the proof of\nCategories, Lemma <REF_0002>\nshows that <MATH_0012> and <MATH_0013> map strongly cartesian morphisms to strongly\ncartesian morphisms, i.e., <MATH_0014> and <MATH_0015> are <MATH_0016>-morphisms of fibred\ncategories over <MATH_0017>. This means that given\n<MATH_0018>, and <MATH_0019> then\nthe presheaves\n<MATH_0020>\nare identified, see\nLemma <REF_0003>. Hence\nthe first is a sheaf if and only if the second is a sheaf.\nFinally, we have to show that if every descent datum in <MATH_0021>\nis effective, then so is every descent datum in <MATH_0022>.\nTo do this, let <MATH_0023> be a descent datum\nin <MATH_0024> relative the covering <MATH_0025> of the site\n<MATH_0026>. Then <MATH_0027> is a descent datum\nin <MATH_0028> relative the covering <MATH_0029>.\nLet <MATH_0030> be an object of <MATH_0031> such that the\ndescent datum <MATH_0032> is isomorphic to\n<MATH_0033>. Then <MATH_0034> is an object of <MATH_0035>\nsuch that the descent datum <MATH_0036> is isomorphic to\n<MATH_0037> which in turn is isomorphic to\nthe original descent datum <MATH_0038> using <MATH_0039>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:27e11f854b7da16882cae70b780e5c9eb14edfeaf31dce1e2eb9e575d8544093", "unit_id": "tag:042W:proof"}
